And then I began to think about it a little bit. And everything we know about elections, we derive from geophysics anyway. Tremors of political change, volcanic elections, political earthquakes. So why not explicitly steal from geophysics? And what we did was we reinterpreted elections in geophysical terms. That is not as Republican versus Democrat, liberal versus conservative or caught versus Reagan. Remember this is 1981, but in earthquake terms, as stability, the party holding the White House keeps the White House and upheaval, the party holding the White House keeps the White House, and upheaval, the party holding the White House is turned out of office.
然后我开始思考这个问题。而且，我们对选举的所有了解，本来就是从地球物理学中衍生出来的。政治变革的震颤，火山般的选举，政治地震。所以，为什么不直接借鉴地球物理学呢？我们所做的，就是用地球物理学的术语来重新解释选举。也就是说，不是将其视为共和党对民主党、自由派对保守派，或是卡特对里根。记住，这是1981年。而是用地震的术语，将其视为稳定——执政党保住白宫，以及剧变——执政党被赶下台。

