administration and it's the governing that really counts. I have nothing against the pollsters. A lot of them are good friends of mine. They're very competent people. But I am saying polls are not predictors. Polls are misused and abused as predictors. I also think that polls lead to lazy and misleading journalism. You don't even have to get out of bed in the morning to write a story about the polls and it leads to this misconception that elections are horse races and it misses all the deeper tides that drive elections. It misses the implications of elections for governance in this country.
行政当局四年的任期内赢或输的，真正重要的是治理。我对民调专家没有任何意见。他们很多人都是我的好朋友。他们是非常称职的人。但我要说的是，民调不是预测器。民调作为预测器被误用和滥用了。我还认为，民调导致了懒惰和误导性的新闻业。你甚至不需要早起下床就能写出一篇关于民调的文章，这导致了一种误解，即选举是赛马，而它忽略了推动选举的所有更深层的潮流。它忽略了选举对这个国家治理的深远影响。

